{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-descartes","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:descartes","kind":"theorem","title":"Descartes theorem","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-brings-is-qou","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-genus-maximal-descent"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-descartes"],"tags":["archimedean-universe","terminal-object","brings-surface"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.descartes","text":"descartes.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:descartes\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}_{-6}</code> denote the category of quantum observable universes over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> satisfying the Descartes condition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi(A) = -6</code>, with morphisms given by QOU maps that preserve the Euler characteristic. Bring's surface <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Sigma_4</code> is a terminal object in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}_{-6}</code>: for every Descartes universe <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{C}_{-6}</code>, there exists a unique morphism to the Bring's QOU.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/descartes.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Theorem","number":"7.14.1"}
